.TH DENIALD 1 "August 2026" "Denial" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
deniald \- run the Denial Wayland compositor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B deniald
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B deniald
owns the DRM/KMS display, input devices, the Wayland frontend, optional
Xwayland integration, and the embedded Flutter desktop scene.
An installed graphical session should normally start
.BR denial-session (1),
which discovers the correct devices, configuration, and Flutter bundle before
invoking this lower-level binary.
.SH SESSION OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-device " path"
Use the DRM card at
.IR path .
.TP
.BI \-\-render-device " path"
Render on a DRM node distinct from the KMS device. Both devices must support a
compatible DMA-BUF format and modifier.
.TP
.BI \-\-output-config " path"
Load persistent output configuration from
.IR path .
.TP
.B \-\-wayland
Start the Wayland frontend and, when available, Xwayland integration.
.TP
.B \-\-no-xwayland
Do not start the Xwayland server or publish an X11
.B DISPLAY
for this session. This option is also accepted by builds compiled without the
optional Xwayland feature.
.TP
.BI \-\-flutter-bundle " path"
Load the packaged Flutter shell bundle from
.IR path .
.TP
.BI \-\-flutter-renderer " skia|impeller"
Select the Flutter GLES renderer. Impeller is the default.
.TP
.B \-\-software-rendering
Select Mesa's
.B kms_swrast
driver and set
.B LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE=1
before initializing GBM, EGL, or Flutter. The installed session launcher uses
this compatibility path automatically for VMware
.BR vmwgfx .
.TP
.B \-\-start-locked
Initialize the native authentication gate and Flutter lock screen as locked.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show all runtime and diagnostic options.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the installed Denial version, immutable candidate build identity, and
Flutter Engine ABI generation.
.SH DIAGNOSTIC OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-frames " count"
Exit after a bounded number of presented frames.
.TP
.BI \-\-commit-seconds " seconds"
Exit after a bounded presentation interval.
.TP
.BI \-\-max-outputs " count"
Limit the outputs used by a controlled KMS run.
.TP
.BI \-\-output-position " name=x,y"
Override an output position for this invocation.
.PP
Additional reconfiguration and topology-test options are listed by
.BR "deniald --help" .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE
Control Mesa's hardware or software renderer selection. The
.B \-\-software-rendering
option sets this to 1 and sets
.B MESA_LOADER_DRIVER_OVERRIDE=kms_swrast
before graphics initialization.
.TP
.B DENIAL_NO_PREDECESSOR=1
Force the session-handoff KMS path without capturing a predecessor framebuffer.
Denial automatically detects direct-boot systems whose primary plane has never
scanned out a framebuffer. This override is intended for unusual DRM
implementations that cannot report or expose their predecessor state. The
default continues to preserve and restore every predecessor framebuffer that
is present during bounded diagnostic runs.
.PP
Denial environment variables use the
.B DENIAL_*
prefix. The former
.B DENIA_*
spellings remain compatibility aliases; the canonical spelling takes
precedence when both are present.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGUSR1
Refresh the embedded packaged Flutter runtime in process.
.TP
.B SIGUSR2
Re-evaluate the live KMS topology.
.TP
.B SIGINT, SIGTERM
Request a bounded compositor shutdown and KMS handoff.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/denial/session.conf
Administrator-owned session and device overrides read by
.BR denial-session (1).
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/denial/outputs.conf
Per-user output configuration initialized and passed by the session launcher.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/denial/flutter
Default installed Flutter shell bundle.
.TP
.I /usr/share/denial/version
Signed-tag runtime version installed only in release packages.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR denial-session (1),
.BR denialctl (1)
